IMPORT prelude

-- A field on only SOME constructors of a type is a PARTIAL field. `rent` is a
-- Tenant's alone; a Landlord has no `rent` at all. So `a's rent` on a value
-- that could still be either is refused when the file is checked — try it by
-- uncommenting the line at the bottom.
--
-- Everything below is a way of telling the checker "here, this value is a
-- Tenant", after which the read is fine.
--
-- One case is NOT checked, and it is the only way a partial read can still
-- fail at run time: a `GIVEN` you left untyped. Every parameter in this file
-- is written `IS AN Actor`, so every read below is checked all the way
-- through. See "What does not narrow" in DECLARE.md for the untyped case.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS addr IS A STRING, name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING, rent IS A NUMBER

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign HAS signer IS AN Actor

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "1 Main St", "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice", 1500
bob         MEANS Tenant OF "Bob", 900
everyone    MEANS LIST theLandlord, alice, bob

-- 1. Take the value apart. The branch you are in tells the checker what `a`
--    is, so the read is legal inside that branch and nowhere else.
GIVEN a IS AN Actor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rent, taken apart` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN Landlord addr name THEN 0
    WHEN Tenant name rent   THEN a's rent

#EVAL `rent, taken apart` alice           -- 1500
#EVAL `rent, taken apart` theLandlord     -- 0

-- 2. Read the payload straight out of the pattern. Shorter, and it needs no
--    projection at all. Usually the one you want.
GIVEN a IS AN Actor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rent, from the pattern` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN Tenant name rent THEN rent
    OTHERWISE 0

#EVAL `rent, from the pattern` alice        -- 1500
#EVAL `rent, from the pattern` theLandlord  -- 0

-- 3. An OTHERWISE gets whatever the branches above it did not take. Landlord
--    is used up above, so only a Tenant can reach here.
GIVEN a IS AN Actor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rent, after OTHERWISE` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN Landlord addr name THEN 0
    OTHERWISE a's rent

#EVAL `rent, after OTHERWISE` alice         -- 1500
#EVAL `rent, after OTHERWISE` theLandlord   -- 0

-- 4. In a quantified rule, name the constructor. `EVERY Tenant t` says the
--    rule ranges over tenants, so `t's rent` in the filter is safe.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`rich tenants sign` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN everyone
        WHO    t's rent AT LEAST 1000
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14

-- A field is an ordinary function, so passing it around is the same partial
-- question written another way, and it is refused the same way. Read the field
-- through a name you have narrowed instead.
#EVAL map (GIVEN x YIELD CONSIDER x
                         WHEN Tenant name rent THEN rent
                         OTHERWISE 0)
          everyone                              -- LIST 0, 1500, 900

-- Uncomment either of these to see the refusal and its explanation.
--
-- GIVEN a IS AN Actor
-- GIVETH A NUMBER
-- `rent, un-narrowed` a MEANS a's rent
--
-- #EVAL map rent everyone
